# Phase 01 roadmap section 30: pre-commit runs the same gate CI runs.
#
# The exit propagation is deliberate and not decoration. Husky does not run the
# hook under `set -e`, so without `|| exit 1` a lint-staged failure would be
# followed by a successful composer ci:check, and the hook would exit 0 on a
# repository it had just failed to format.
#
# lint-staged comes first so the fixes it applies are inside the commit rather
# than sitting in the working tree waiting for the next attempt.
#
# The full gate costs about 22 seconds locally, and most of that is the 265
# test suite. That is a deliberate trade: a commit is rejected on a red test
# rather than being pushed and found red afterwards. It also means committing
# requires the MySQL test database to be up. Use --no-verify when that is not
# the situation.
#
# @see docs/DECISIONS.md D-28
npx lint-staged || exit 1
composer ci:check